# Features & UI

## Routes stay thin

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
export const Route = createFileRoute("/_authenticated/")({
  component: Page,
});
function Page() {
  const { user } = Route.useRouteContext();
  return <ChatApp user={user} />;
}

// ❌ BAD — large UI / Zero logic inside the route file
```

## Feature structure

```
features/chat/
  ui/          # React components
  lib/         # pure helpers, types, pagination
  index.ts     # public exports only
```

- Pass data and callbacks as props; avoid deep imports across features.
- Prefer shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `ScrollArea`, …) over custom one-off controls.
- Import UI: `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`.
- Import app code: `import { ChatApp } from "#/features/chat"`.
- Do not edit generated `routeTree.gen.ts`.
- Theme tokens live in `src/styles.css`; map new shadcn vars to existing brand tokens instead of inventing a second palette.
